{
  "id": "ep118",
  "duration": 51.467,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.102,
      "text": "One tiny moon looks like a jigsaw puzzle glued back together.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Miranda as seen by Voyager 2 - GPN-2003-000005.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miranda_as_seen_by_Voyager_2_-_GPN-2003-000005.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.102,
      "end": 11.972,
      "text": "When Voyager 2 reached Uranus in 1986, scientists expected its moon Miranda to be a boring ice-ball.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Uranus2.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uranus2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.1,
          "end": 11.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.972,
      "end": 18.792,
      "text": "Instead, they found a 'Frankenstein' world of mismatched geological blocks and a massive V-shaped scar.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Miranda elsinorinverness.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miranda_elsinorinverness.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.967,
          "end": 15.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 15.4,
          "end": 18.8,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.792,
      "end": 25.042,
      "text": "Miranda\u2019s surface features Verona Rupes, a staggering cliff reaching up to twelve miles deep.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Miranda scarp.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miranda_scarp.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.8,
          "end": 21.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 21.933,
          "end": 25.033,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.042,
      "end": 30.687,
      "text": "That is twelve times deeper than the Grand Canyon, on a world barely the size of Texas.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Rain over Grand Canyon.jpg",
        "credit": "Romain Guy from San Francisco, USA",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rain_over_Grand_Canyon.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.033,
          "end": 27.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 27.867,
          "end": 30.7,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.687,
      "end": 37.932,
      "text": "One leading theory suggests this chaotic moon was shattered by impacts multiple times before reassembling.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist's concept of collision at HD 172555.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%27s_concept_of_collision_at_HD_172555.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.7,
          "end": 34.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 34.033,
          "end": 37.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.932,
      "end": 45.682,
      "text": "Alternatively, extreme tidal heating from Uranus might have churned the moon's icy interior into these bizarre shapes.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "11214 2023 990 Fig1 HTML.webp",
        "credit": "by David Hinkle (JPL)\n\nin Roberts, J.H., McKinnon, W.B., Elder, C.M.\u00a0et al.\u00a0Exploring the Interior of Europa with the Europa Clipper.\u00a0Space Sci Rev\u00a0219, 46 (2023). https://doi.org/10.1007/s11214-023-0",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:11214_2023_990_Fig1_HTML.webp"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.933,
          "end": 45.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 45.682,
      "end": 51.117,
      "text": "Since we have only photographed its southern half, the rest of the jigsaw puzzle remains a mystery.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Miranda as seen by Voyager 2 - GPN-2003-000005.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miranda_as_seen_by_Voyager_2_-_GPN-2003-000005.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 45.667,
          "end": 51.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
